From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lethalbas <lethalbas@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:25:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add clean-room KTX 2.0 container reader (Ktx2Reader)

New GPL-2.0-only reader written only from the Khronos KTX 2.0
specification (KTX-Specification commit ac39917e) and the public zstd
API. It does not use or derive from libktx.

- validates identifier, vkFormat, dimensions, texture type, levelCount,
  supercompression scheme, DFD/KVD/SGD ranges (in file, non-overlapping),
  key/value entries, and every level's offset/length/order against the
  file size and the size implied by format and dimensions
- overflow-checked arithmetic; caller-provided limits bound allocations
- supercompression: none and Zstandard; BasisLZ, ZLIB and vendor schemes
  and VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED are rejected as unsupported
- inflated level data is returned base level first, each level aligned
  to lcm(texel block size, 4); vkFormat is passed through

Ktx2FormatTable.inl is generated by Tools/GenKtx2FormatTable.py from the
spec's formats.json and the Vulkan SDK 1.4.363 headers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
